  "articleBody": "So, you're tackling an interior wall project, huh? It's exciting to imagine that new layout, but a few common missteps can really throw a wrench in things. One big one is not checking for square and plumb; if your walls aren't straight up and down, or perfectly level, everything that comes after (like drywall and trim) will look off. Trust me, you'll notice it. Another frequent issue is ignoring your existing ceiling and floor. These aren't always perfectly even, and if you don't account for those irregularities, your new wall can end up looking wavy or forced. It’s also super easy to misplace openings or where one wall meets another, leading to headaches later. You might think you can just eyeball it, but precise measurements and planning are your best friends here. And don't forget about those pesky building permits! Depending on where you are, even a non-load-bearing wall might need one, and skipping that can lead to fines or having to tear it all down. When in doubt, it’s always smart to have a professional eye on things, especially if the project feels a bit over your head. Here at HH Remodeling, we've seen it all, and we can help you avoid these pitfalls.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
